{
  "name": "HB Briefing",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "focus": "regulatory action and litigation in telecoms and internet service provision. That is its core: enforcement by regulators (FCC, FTC, state attorneys general, public utility commissions), and lawsuits, settlements, rulings, consent orders and appeals involving ISPs, fibre builders, cable operators and their investors",
  "secondary": "ISP billing disputes, unreturned-equipment scams, deceptive or hidden fees, municipal broadband politics, BEAD and universal-service funding, spectrum policy, and consumer data breaches",
  "briefing_interest": "regulatory action and litigation affecting telecoms and ISPs: who is being investigated, sued, fined, forced into a settlement, or handed a ruling, and what it means next",
  "deep_always_relevant": "A regulatory proceeding or lawsuit described in the text",
  "severity_high": "a live proceeding or enforcement outcome (suit filed, ruling, fine, settlement, consent order)",
  "severity_medium": "investigation, inquiry, proposed rule, or a named matter under watch",
  "severity_low": "background analysis or opinion",
  "excluded": "Vendor marketing, product reviews, comparison listicles, index/database pages, login pages and generic how-tos",
